{"content":"Perfect. I have all the information I need to answer the question.\n\nq27.\n\n**Mechanism:** Go `embed` (compile-time file embedding)\n\n**Path:** `server/router/frontend/frontend.go`\n\nThe compiled React frontend is served in production through Go's built-in `embed` package (line 20-21 of `server/router/frontend/frontend.go`), which embeds the contents of the `server/router/frontend/dist/` directory directly into the compiled binary at build time. The `FrontendService.Serve()` method registers this embedded filesystem with the Echo HTTP server using middleware (line 54-59) to serve static assets and the SPA fallback, eliminating the need for separate static file deployment.\n\nThe React build process outputs to `server/router/frontend/dist/` via `pnpm release` in `web/package.json` (line 11), ensuring the compiled frontend files are present before the Go binary is built.","iteration":10,"turn":1,"type":"assistant"}
